s.push(A.iV("\u0cb5\u0cbf\u0c82\u0cb6\u0ccb\u0ca4\u0ccd\u0ca4\u0cb0\u0cbf \u0ca6\u0cb6 / Vimshottari Dasha"))
s.push(A.nj("Vimshottari Dasha is a 120-year planetary period system based on the Moon's Nakshatra at birth.\n\n\ud83d\udd11 Start Point: The balance of the Dasha at birth is calculated from how far the Moon has traversed its birth Nakshatra.\n\nBalance = (1 \u2212 nakshatra_traversed_fraction) \xd7 lord's_total_years\n\nDasha Lords and their periods (total 120 years):\nKetu 7 \u2022 Venus 20 \u2022 Sun 6 \u2022 Moon 10 \u2022 Mars 7 \u2022 Rahu 18 \u2022 Jupiter 16 \u2022 Saturn 19 \u2022 Mercury 17\n\n\ud83d\udcca Antardasha (sub-periods) are calculated by proportional subdivision: each Mahadasha is split into 9 Antardashas in the same lord sequence, proportional to period lengths.",B.UO,"Planetary Period System"))
s.push(B.bx)
s.push(A.iV("\u0cb7\u0ca1\u0ccd\u0cac\u0cb2 / Shadbala"))
s.push(A.nj("Shadbala measures the total strength of each planet in 6 categories, expressed in Rupas and Shashtiamshas:\n\n1. Sthana Bala (\u0cb8\u0ccd\u0ca5\u0cbe\u0ca8 \u0cac\u0cb2) \u2014 Positional strength: Uccha (exaltation), Saptavargaja (divisional chart placement), Ojayugmarashyamsha, Kendradi, and Drekkana strengths.\n\n2. Dig Bala (\u0ca6\u0cbf\u0c97\u0ccd \u0cac\u0cb2) \u2014 Directional strength. Each planet is strongest in a specific house quadrant.\n\n3. Kala Bala (\u0c95\u0cbe\u0cb2 \u0cac\u0cb2) \u2014 Temporal strength: Natonnata (day/night), Paksha (lunar fortnight), Tribhaga, Abda, Masa, Vara, Hora, Ayana, and Yuddha (planetary war).\n\n4. Chesta Bala (\u0c9a\u0cc7\u0cb7\u0ccd\u0c9f \u0cac\u0cb2) \u2014 Motional strength based on retrograde/direct motion and speed.\n\n5. Naisargika Bala (\u0ca8\u0cc8\u0cb8\u0cb0\u0ccd\u0c97\u0cbf\u0c95 \u0cac\u0cb2) \u2014 Natural/inherent strength: Fixed order: Saturn < Mars < Mercury < Jupiter < Venus < Moon < Sun.\n\n6. Drik Bala (\u0ca6\u0cc3\u0c95\u0ccd \u0cac\u0cb2) \u2014 Aspectual strength from other planets.\n\nMinimum required Rupas benchmarks are used to evaluate whether each planet meets its strength threshold.",B.TM,"6-Fold Planetary Strength"))
s.push(B.bx)
s.push(A.iV("\u0cb5\u0cb0\u0ccd\u0c97 \u0c9a\u0c95\u0ccd\u0cb0\u0c97\u0cb3\u0cc1 / Divisional Charts"))
s.push(A.nj("Each planet's sign is subdivided into smaller equal segments:\n\n\u2022 D-1 (Rashi/Lagna chart) \u2014 Full 30\xb0 of each sign. The primary chart.\n\n\u2022 D-9 (Navamsha) \u2014 Each sign is divided into 9 equal parts of 3\xb020'. The Navamsha describes the inner nature of the planet and is crucial for assessing marriage and dharma.\n\n\u2022 D-12 (Dwadashamsha) \u2014 Each sign is divided into 12 equal parts of 2\xb030'. Used to assess parents and ancestral karma.\n\n\u2022 D9 of D9 \u2014 The Navamsha within the Navamsha, giving a deeper sub-divisional reading.",B.UK,"D-1, D-9, D-12 Subdivisions"))
s.push(B.bx)
s.push(A.iV("\u0c86\u0cb0\u0cc2\u0ca2 \u0cb2\u0c97\u0ccd\u0ca8 / Arudha Lagna"))
s.push(A.nj("The Arudha Lagna represents how the world perceives you \u2014 the image or Maya you project.\n\n\ud83d\udcd0 Calculation:\n1. Count houses from Lagna to its lord.\n2. Count the same number of houses from the lord.\n3. The resulting house is the Arudha Lagna.\n\nException: If the result falls in the 1st or 7th house from Lagna, move it 10 houses forward (classical Parashari rule).\n\nThe app calculates Arudhas for all 12 Bhavas (A1\u2013A12) using this same method applied to each house lord.",B.UE,"Maya & Manifestation"))
s.push(B.bx)
s.push(A.iV("\u0ca4\u0cbe\u0cb0\u0cbe\u0ca8\u0cc1\u0c95\u0cc2\u0cb2 / Taranukula"))
s.push(A.nj("Taranukula evaluates the 27 Nakshatras relative to the Janma (birth) Nakshatra using a 9-fold cycle:\n\n1. Janma (Birth) \u2014 The Nakshatra itself.\n2. Sampat (Wealth)\n3. Vipat (Danger/Loss)\n4. Kshema (Well-being)\n5. Pratyak (Obstacle)\n6. Sadhana (Achievement)\n7. Naidhana (Death/End)\n8. Mitra (Friend)\n9. Parama Mitra (Best Friend)\n\nThe cycle repeats every 9 Nakshatras. Beneficial: Sampat, Kshema, Sadhana, Mitra, Parama Mitra.\nInauspicious: Vipat, Pratyak, Naidhana.",B.UN,"Star Compatibility from Birth Nakshatra"))
s.push(B.bx)
s.push(A.iV("\u0cae\u0cc7\u0cb3\u0cbe\u0caa\u0c95 / Melapaka (Compatibility)"))
s.push(A.nj("Melapaka assesses marriage compatibility by comparing the Rashi and Nakshatra of two people across 8 Kootas:\n\n1. Varna (1 pt) \u2014 Spiritual compatibility by caste category.\n2. Vashya (2 pt) \u2014 Control/dominance relationship between signs.\n3. Tara (3 pt) \u2014 Star compatibility using the Taranukula cycle.\n4. Yoni (4 pt) \u2014 Sexual/physical compatibility by animal symbols.\n5. Graha Maitri (5 pt) \u2014 Friendship between Moon sign lords.\n6. Gana (6 pt) \u2014 Nature: Deva (divine), Manushya (human), Rakshasa (demon).\n7. Rashi (7 pt) \u2014 Sign compatibility (Bhakuta): positive/negative relationships between Rashis.\n8. Nadi (8 pt) \u2014 Energy channel: Vata, Pitta, Kapha. Same Nadi = 0 points (Nadi Dosha).\n\nMaximum = 36 points. Score \u2265 18 is considered compatible.",B.U3,"36-Point Marriage Compatibility"))
s.push(B.bx)
s.push(A.iV("\u0c89\u0caa\u0c97\u0ccd\u0cb0\u0cb9\u0c97\u0cb3\u0cc1 / Upagrahas & Special Points"))
s.push(A.nj("\ud83d\udd34 Mandi & Gulika: Calculated from sunrise/sunset times and the hora (planetary hour) sequence for the day. Mandi is the son of Saturn and is considered inauspicious.\n\n\u2b50 Advanced Sphutas (16 points) include:\n\u2022 Bhava Lagna, Hora Lagna, Ghati Lagna \u2014 time-based Lagnas.\n\u2022 Pushkara Navamsha & Bhaga \u2014 auspicious sub-divisions.\n\u2022 Shree Lagna, Indu Lagna, Pranapada \u2014 derived special ascendants.\n\u2022 Varnada Lagna \u2014 used for Varna calculation in Jaimini.\n\u2022 Yogi, Avayogi, Duplicate Yogi \u2014 fortune/misfortune points calculated from Sun + Moon longitude + 93\xb020'.",B.UD,"Mandi, Gulika & 16 Sphutas"))
s.push(B.an)
